#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124205 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "ccfdc303-534f-530e-810b-f475a997f5d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4703" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124206 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/id #uuid "22a77802-4114-516f-a0e0-4cda2e069361" :question/math-academy-id "e-4704" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124207 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6e4b2e85-86a8-5050-a60a-ae8d40453ad0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4705" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124208 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "3ac076bd-5add-5c08-bb96-7b11c0a37d54" :question/math-academy-id "e-4706" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{2}{7}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "957a4605-c594-58ef-b362-91223f6b17ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308341} {:answer/id #uuid "d625f55b-7755-5755-bcdf-e09776f1552c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308342} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1a2e02-dbdf-5217-93ac-e2b2aaab15bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, $4$th, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308343} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd0da23-66a4-5659-aebe-8fc00c40f78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All the columns are pivot" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308344} {:answer/id #uuid "53132b96-b03c-5230-8c37-a905a667c2b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb1a2e02-dbdf-5217-93ac-e2b2aaab15bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, $4$th, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308343} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec78d2ac-4d04-5e06-949d-b9663c624632" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe1c5404-bbff-566c-b120-dde7595ffb3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130946" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -9 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ ha