ademy-id "q-130949" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd388027-a8a2-528b-bf03-e88def5e5342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308362} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6fd2b3-45d0-5e58-b0aa-692dad466fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308363} {:answer/id #uuid "53f461f8-661e-57e7-9fb3-36785436b09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308364} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a9b3dc-235a-5fbb-b30a-570e4367f915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308365} {:answer/id #uuid "fd87c074-df5d-543b-9d99-bdd0d8f70dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53f461f8-661e-57e7-9fb3-36785436b09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308364} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e1ca980-1779-5c78-918f-8047e2925787" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d08fdd6f-e7ad-5c58-bb46-64ef9f075371" :question/math-academy-id "q-130951" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $R$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $R$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $4$th column."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "287b38ee-41c7-5532-a8a3-471340d911f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308369} {:answer/id #uuid "63026364-bf1b-50ac-b117-cbf42d7f36cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308370} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb0ec5a-6781-5d33-9e7b-73e42215938b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308371} {:answer/id #uuid "ee04422b-9124-56c2-9b98-4a81d3395c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308372} {:answer/id #uuid "2f74ad50-7430-5dbc-84ac-d80c7e1bcc93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bb0